From a58efebbedbbeccb4f6083c22d4be999f150bcf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alfonso Fortunato <57877156+devopsfortunato@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:15:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add opt-in MXFP8 LM head via VLLM_MXFP8_LM_HEAD (fork
 parity)

Ports the fork's runtime LM head quantization. With VLLM_MXFP8_LM_HEAD=1 (default off), an
unquantized BF16 ParallelLMHead on a Blackwell 12x device with the b12x MXFP8 linear kernel stores
its weight as MXFP8 (block-32 scales) and runs the logits GEMM on b12x with BF16 activations, as
the fork's default VLLM_LM_HEAD_A16=1 does. Checks: BF16 model and params, K%128 == 0,
N per rank %8 == 0, linear backend auto/b12x, head not tied, B12xMxfp8LinearKernel selected.
Applies to the target head and the MTP drafter's own head.

The head loads exactly like an unquantized one (_LMHeadBF16Source as the requantization source of
Mxfp8OnlineLinearMethod) and is quantized once after loading. The online method's own meta-device
loading does not fit the vocab-parallel loader: the first version of this patch served flat logits
(every token "!"). online_quantization_timing_context now skips timing for a layer without a quant
config instead of asserting.

Measured on one DGX Spark with patches 18-19: decode 40.47 -> 45.45 t/s (dbench geomean), output
text normal, perplexity 1.0872 / 2.2090 / 1.0454 against the fork image's 1.0902 / 2.2049 / 1.0470.
